-- Source module: Solutions.R6Params
/-!
# Round six: the parameter map `n ↦ (b, b', p, L, T, d, ℓ, r, K, α², V)` and the cost `Ncost6`

Stack parameters (Colkitt/Jain, `stack-notes.tex` §1 Idea D, Idea C):

* `b = lg n` (`bP6`), `b' = b^(1+x)` (`b'P6`; `x : ℕ` so `⌈b^(1+x)⌉ = b^(1+x)`), `p = 6 b'` (`pP6`);
* `L` (`LP6`) = least `L` with `4n ≤ 2^L b'`, `T = 2^L` (`TP6`), so `4n ≤ T b' < 8n`;
* `d = ⌊b^ε⌋` (`dP6`), `ℓ = ⌈L/d⌉ = (L + d - 1)/d` (`ℓP6`), `r = 2^ℓ` (`rP6`),
  `K = ℓ - 1` (`KP6`, one chunk per axis);
* `α² = ⌊p/(48d)⌋ = ⌊b'/(8d)⌋` (`α2P6`, a natural number), `α = √(α²)` (`αP6`),
  `γ = 2 d α²` (`γP6`);
* bit volume `V = T p` (`VP6`), with `24 n ≤ V ≤ 48 n`.

## Normalization (same as OpenAI's `RCost.Ncost`)
`Ncost6` is the **per-bit** cost: the Table-1 cost divided by `V = T p`.  The machine time is
`C₀ (V · Ncost6 · polylog + n)`; since `V ≤ 48 n`, a bound `Ncost6 ≤ C b^(1-gap) polylog`
gives time `O(n lg^(1-gap) polylog)`.

`Ncost6 P n = d + ℓ d^λ' + d p^δ + (ℓ + log₂ p) + p^δ + ℓ (d ln p)^τ + 1`
(rows: prefix moves `1-ε`; butterflies `ε(1-λ')`; fine exposures/Gaussian/chirps/reserved axes
`1-ε-poly`; pointwise products `ε`; precision `p^δ = b^poly`; CRT reversal
`ε(1-τ) = max(ε,1-ε)(1-τ)` as `ε ≥ 1/2`).  Note `ℓ ≈ b^(1-ε)` and `p^δ ≤ 6 b^poly`.
-/

